@*
    WizardSection — shared numbered-card primitive for the six wizards.
    M.2d.1 deliverable per the v2 plan §5.2 (round-1 #2 — the most useful
    missing primitive surfaced in ChatGPT review).

    Responsibilities (chrome only):
      * MudPaper wrapper with consistent elevation + padding + margin.
      * Numbered title — "{Index}. {Title}".
      * Optional description text rendered as a caption.
      * ChildContent slot — the section body.

    What this is NOT responsible for (anti-coupling lock — round-2 #10):
      * Field layout — wizards decide MudGrid / table / flex / charts /
        custom panes inside ChildContent. WizardSection does NOT wrap
        ChildContent in MudGrid.

    DoD §6 anti-layout-coupling check: this file contains zero
    MudGrid constructs.

    Reference: docs/sessions/2026-05-21-m2d1-shared-primitives-plan-v2.md §5.2
*@

<MudPaper Elevation="1" Class="pa-4 mb-4" data-testid="wizard-section">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Style="font-weight:500;" Class="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Description) ? "mb-3" : "mb-1")"
             data-testid="wizard-section-title">@Index. @Title</MudText>
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Description))
    {
        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-3" data-testid="wizard-section-description">@Description</MudText>
    }
    @ChildContent
</MudPaper>

@code {
    /// <summary>Section number rendered as the title prefix (e.g. <c>1. Identity</c>).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Index { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Section title text.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional help text rendered as a small caption directly below the
    /// numbered title. When null or empty, no caption is rendered.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Description { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The section body. Wizards decide the inner layout (MudGrid for
    /// field grids, plain markup for tables, panes, charts, etc.).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
